; Tutorial 1.03: Making Decisions
;
; Programs become interesting when they do different things in different situations. If and Select choose which
; code runs.
;
; Works on: the original Blitz3D and BlitzPlus, and BlitzLLVM.

Graphics 800, 600, 0, 2 ; A bigger window, so that everything printed fits.

; --- Comparing values ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; A comparison is either true (1) or false (0):
;   =  equal          <>  not equal
;   <  less           <=  less or equal
;   >  greater        >=  greater or equal
Print "5 > 3 is " + (5 > 3)
Print "5 = 3 is " + (5 = 3)
Print "True is " + True + ", False is " + False

; --- If ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Rnd and Rand make random numbers (tutorial 1.09). Here we roll a six-sided die.
SeedRnd MilliSecs()
Local roll = Rand(1, 6)
Print
Print "You rolled a " + roll + "."

; The short form fits on one line.
If roll = 6 Then Print "A six! Roll again."

; The long form can hold many lines, and ends with EndIf.
If roll >= 4
	Print "That is a high roll."
	Print "Move forward " + roll + " spaces."
Else
	Print "That is a low roll."
EndIf

; ElseIf checks another condition when the ones before it were false. Only the first true branch runs.
Local temperature = Rand(-10, 40)
Print
Print "It is " + temperature + " degrees outside."
If temperature < 0
	Print "Wear a thick coat."
ElseIf temperature < 15
	Print "Take a jacket."
ElseIf temperature < 28
	Print "A T-shirt is fine."
Else
	Print "Find some shade."
EndIf

; --- And, Or, Not ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; And is true when both sides are true. Or is true when at least one side is. Not flips true and false.
Local hasKey = Rand(0, 1)
Local doorLocked = Rand(0, 1)
Print
Print "Has key: " + hasKey + ", door locked: " + doorLocked
If (Not doorLocked) Or hasKey ; Brackets make the order clear: Not first, then Or.
	Print "You can open the door."
Else
	Print "The door will not open."
EndIf

; Any number that is not 0 counts as true, so you can test a value directly.
Local coins = Rand(0, 3)
If coins Then Print "You have " + coins + " coins." Else Print "Your pockets are empty."

; --- Select ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Select compares one value against many cases. It is easier to read than a long ElseIf chain.
Local day = Rand(1, 7)
Print
Select day
	Case 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 ; One case can list several values.
		Print "Day " + day + " is a work day."
	Case 6
		Print "Day 6 is Saturday."
	Case 7
		Print "Day 7 is Sunday."
	Default ; Runs when no case matched.
		Print "That is not a day."
End Select

; Run the program a few times: the random numbers give a different story each time.
Print
Print "Press any key to quit."
WaitKey
End
